@@ -0,0 +1,214 @@
+# Architecture overview
+
+This document describes how the `xui` crates layer, how data flows through a
+single frame, and how the rendering pipeline is structured. For the public API
+of each crate, see the [per-crate docs](./README.md).
+
+## Layering
+
+The workspace is intentionally split so that foundational types have no
+dependency on the runtime or backends. Dependencies point downward only.
+
+```text
+application crate
+    │
+    ├──► xui                      core runtime, fiber, hooks, layout, widgets, scene
+    │       │
+    │       ├──► xui-interface    shared types (geometry, style, events, text traits)
+    │       ├──► xui-animation    Tween / Animatable (depends on interface + macros)
+    │       ├──► xui-text         optional text layout (depends on interface)
+    │       └──► slot             generational slot storage with RenderPhase guards
+    │
+    ├──► xui-components           built-in widgets (depends on xui)
+    │
+    ├──► xui-text-engine          cosmic-text impl of interface text traits
+    │
+    ├──► xui-skia                 Skia backend (depends on xui, interface, render-graph)
+    │
+    └──► xui-winit                winit window/event loop (depends on xui, interface,
+                                 render-graph, text-engine; selects skia or wgpu)
+```
+
+Backends (`xui-skia`, optional `wgpu` in `xui-winit`) implement the
+`xui::render::RenderBackend` and `xui_interface::TextBackend` traits. The core
+runtime never names a GPU library directly.
+
+## Crate roles by concern
+
+### Types and contracts — `xui-interface`
+
+The shared vocabulary every other crate agrees on:
+
+- **Geometry** — `Color`, `Point`, `Rect`, `Size`, `Sizing`, `EdgeInsets`,
+  `Bounds`, `Translation`.
+- **Style** — `Style`, `StylePatch`, `ComputedStyle`, `*StylePatch` per layer
+  (layout, paint, text, scroll, transform, effect), tokens (`ColorToken`,
+  `SpacingToken`, `FontSizeToken`, `RadiusToken`), `Theme`, `WidgetStateMatcher`
+  for state rules.
+- **Events** — raw window/pointer/keyboard events (`RawWindowEvent`,
+  `RawPointerButton`, `RawKeyboard`, `RawWheel`, …), semantic requests
+  (`EventRequest`, `EventRequests`), shortcuts (`Shortcut`, `ShortcutBinding`).
+- **Widget** — `Component`, `NodeId`, `Key`, `WidgetType`, `AccessibilityRole`.
+- **Platform** — `TextInputSession`, `PlatformOutput`.
+- **Transition** — `Easing`, `Transition`, `AnimationProgress`.
+- **Text traits** — `TextBackend`, `Shaper`, `FontDatabase`, `GlyphRasterizer`,
+  plus layout data (`ParagraphLayout`, `LineLayout`, `GlyphRun`, …).
+- **Dirty tracking** — `WidgetUpdateFlags`, `StyleDiffFlags`.
+
+### Runtime and reconciler — `xui`
+
+The heart of the framework:
+
+- **`runtime::GuiRuntime`** — drives the event/render loop, owns the
+  `TextHost`, `ShortcutManager`, and `EventSource`.
+- **`app::App`** — owns the component root, tokio async runtime, scheduler,
+  theme, and `TextHost`; renders frames through a `RenderBackend`.
+- **`fiber`** — retained fiber tree keyed by `FiberId` (slotmap); reconciles
+  `ElementDesc` trees into a widget/layout tree.
+- **`state`** — hooks (`HookContext`, `Memo`, `Resource`, `Callback`,
+  `AsyncValue`, `TaskContext`), lanes for batched updates, scheduler and async
+  dispatcher. Uses `slot` for phase-guarded storage.
+- **`lanes`** — update lanes (default, retry, …) for concurrent and batched
+  state propagation.
+- **`layout`** — `taffy` flexbox over retained spatial nodes.
+- **`style`** — merges patches/tokens/themes into `ComputedStyle`, applies
+  `WidgetStateMatcher` rules.
+- **`render`** — backend-independent scene (`RenderNodeId`, `PictureId`,
+  `PrimitiveId`), scene compiler, compiled scene, and `RenderBackend` trait.
+- **`widgets`** — primitive widget interface (`WidgetI`) and built-in primitives
+  (text, container, scroll, overlay).
+- **`event_system`** — translates raw events into semantic events and dispatches
+  callbacks; focus manager; shortcut manager.
+- **`assets`** — installs the process-global `AssetManager` and exposes
+  `load_image_asset` and friends.
+- **`element`** — `ElementDesc`, `ComponentDesc`, `WidgetDesc`, `portal`.
+
+### Macros — `xui-macros`
+
+Compile-time DSLs that produce `ElementDesc` / `Style` / components:
+
+- `xui! { <Tag attr={expr}>{children}</Tag> }` → `ElementDesc`.
+- `style!(padding: 16.0, background: if hovered { ... })` → `Style` with
+  state-conditioned rules lowered to `WidgetStateMatcher`.
+- `#[component]` / `component_fn!` — generates a props struct, a typed builder,
+  a support module, and a `ComponentRender` handle.
+- `#[main]` — includes the asset bootstrap module and installs the
+  `AssetManager` before the user's `main` body runs.
+- `#[derive(Animatable)]` — field-wise `Animatable` impl.
+
+### Animation — `xui-animation`
+
+`Animatable` trait + derive, `Tween<T>`, `Timeline`, `AnimationClock`.
+Interpolations for `f32`, `NotNan<f32>`, `Point`, `Size`, `EdgeInsets`,
+`Color`, `LengthValue`, `ColorValue`, `ColorStyle`, gradients, shadows,
+strokes, scrollbars. Discrete variant switches are snap-at-end.
+
+### Components — `xui-components`
+
+Built-in widgets built on top of `xui`: `button`, `input` (wraps
+`text_input`), `dropdown`, `tabs`, `image`, `icon` (SVG/path icons),
+`virtual_list`, and shared layout helpers (`ComponentLength`, `ComponentSizing`,
+`ComponentInsets`, `ComponentColor`).
+
+## Per-frame data flow
+
+```text
+winit events
+    │
+    ▼
+xui_winit::translate_window_event   ──►  RawEvent (xui_interface::events)
+    │
+    ▼
+GuiRuntime  ──►  App
+    │
+    ├─ event lane:  raw events → EventTranslator → semantic events / callbacks
+    │
+    ├─ effect lane: run pending effects, async task wakeups (tokio)
+    │
+    └─ render phase (slot::RenderPhase::Render):
+         │
+         ├─ re-render dirty components via HookContext → ElementDesc tree
+         │
+         ├─ fiber reconciler diffs ElementDesc → retained widget + layout tree
+         │
+         ├─ style system: patches + theme + state → ComputedStyle per node
+         │
+         ├─ taffy layout pass → node Bounds
+         │
+        ── scene built (RenderNodeId / PictureId / PrimitiveId)
+         │
+         ├─ scene compiler → render graph (xui-render-graph LayerProgram)
+         │
+        ── backend (xui-skia SkiaBackend / wgpu) rasterizes frame → surface
+         │
+        ── TextBackend (xui-text-engine CosmicEngine) lays out & rasterizes glyphs
+```
+
+State reads/writes are phase-checked (see `slot`): hook storage may only be
+written during `Event`/`Effect` phases and read during any active phase.
+Debug builds assert this.
+
+## Rendering pipeline
+
+The render path is split into three stages so backends stay thin:
+
+1. **Scene** (`xui::render::scene`) — a retained, backend-independent tree of
+   layers, pictures, and primitives. Spatial nodes track transforms/clips.
+2. **Render graph** (`xui-render-graph`) — `compile_layer` normalizes static
+   style into a reusable `LayerProgram`; `LayerProgram::instantiate` applies
+   frame geometry, lowers executable pass IR, and assigns abstract transient
+   texture slots. Pure Rust, no GPU dependency, `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`.
+3. **Backend** (`xui-skia`, or `wgpu` via `xui-winit`) — consumes the graph and
+   rasterizes to the window surface. `xui-skia` uses `skia-safe` with Metal on
+   macOS; caches layers, glyphs, and paragraphs; reports frame stats.
+
+## Asset pipeline
+
+```text
+xui.toml  ──►  xui-cli (cargo xui)  ──►  xui-pak-build
+                                              │
+                                  writes .xpak + xui_asset_refs.rs
+                                              │
+                                  bootstrap module (xui_assets::refs + manager())
+                                              │
+                                  XUI_ASSETS_BOOTSTRAP env → xui::include_assets!()
+                                              │
+                                  xui_assets::manager() → AssetManager (xui-assets)
+                                              │
+                                  mount order: DirectorySource (dev) → EmbeddedPak / PakSource
+```
+
+- `xui-pak` defines the `.xpak` format: fixed header, payload blobs (zstd or
+  none), postcard index, blake3 content hashes, power-of-two alignment.
+- `xui-pak-build` scans a source directory with `ignore`, applies glob rules,
+  encodes a deterministic archive, and generates Rust asset-id constants.
+- `xui-assets` `AssetManager` searches mounted sources in insertion order
+  (first match wins), caches decompressed immutable bytes, and parses via
+  `AssetFormat`. `DirectorySource` is `Volatile` (live edits); paks are
+  `Immutable` (cached, zero-copy `AssetBytes::Mapped`/`Static`).
+- `xui-cli` orchestrates all of the above from `xui.toml` and invokes Cargo.
+
+## State storage
+
+Two cooperating primitives back hook state:
+
+- **`slot`** — `Scope`/`Pointer`/`Storage` with a thread-local `RenderPhase`
+  (`Render`/`Event`/`Effect`/`Commit`). Debug builds assert reads/writes happen
+  in a legal phase. Used directly by `xui::state`.
+- **`xui-slot`** — `GenerationalBox<T, S>` with `UnsyncStorage`/`SyncStorage`
+  and an `Owner` that drops its boxes on drop. Reference-counted variants and
+  `Owner::insert_reference` support signal-style sharing.
+
+## Backend selection
+
+`xui-winit` exposes feature flags:
+
+```toml
+[dependencies]
+xui-winit = { path = "../xui-winit", features = ["skia"] }   # default
+# or
+xui-winit = { path = "../xui-winit", default-features = false, features = ["wgpu"] }
+```
+
+`skia` pulls in `xui-skia` and re-exports `SkiaBackend`; `wgpu` pulls in the
+optional `wgpu` renderer module (`TexturePool`, `WGPUBackend`, …).

diff --git a/docs/crates/slot.md b/docs/crates/slot.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9c71261
--- a/docs/crates/slot.md
+++ b/docs/crates/slot.md
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+# `slot` — generational slot storage with phase guards
+
+A small, focused storage primitive used by `xui::state` for hook-local
+scratch storage. It combines a generational `Pointer`/`Scope` allocator with a
+thread-local `RenderPhase` guard so that, in debug builds, state reads and
+writes are only permitted during legal runtime phases.
+
+## Public API
+
+### `RenderPhase` and `Runtime`
+
+```rust
+pub enum RenderPhase { Render, Event, Effect, Commit }
+```
+
+- `Runtime::new(phase)` / `enter(f)` / `with_phase(phase, f)` — set the
+  thread-local current phase for the duration of a closure (RAII guard restores
+  the previous phase).
+- `Runtime::current_render_phase()` — read the active phase.
+- `RenderPhase::allows_slot_read()` (always `true` while a phase is active) and
+  `allows_slot_write()` (`true` only for `Event`/`Effect`).
+
+Debug builds assert slot reads require an active phase and slot writes require
+a write-capable phase.
+
+### `Pointer<S, T>`
+
+A `Copy` generational handle: `(NonNull<S>, generation: u64)`. `Eq`/`Hash` by
+slot address + generation. `try_read` / `try_write` go through the `Storage`
+trait and carry the same debug phase assertions.
+
+### `Storage` and `ScopeStorage` traits
+
+- `Storage<Data>` — `try_read(Pointer) -> Result<Ref<'static, T>>` and
+  `try_write(Pointer) -> Result<Mut<'static, T>>` (unsafe, phase-checked).
+- `ScopeStorage` — `allocate`, `recycle`, `remove`, `contains`, `clear`
+  (unsafe; ownership is checked by the owning `Scope`).
+
+### `Scope<S: ScopeStorage>`
+
+Owns a `Vec<NonNull<S>>` of allocated slots. `insert(value) -> Pointer`,
+`remove(pointer) -> Result<T>`, `contains(pointer) -> bool`, `clear()` (drops
+all and recycles). `Drop` clears the scope. `Scope::new()` is the unsync
+default.
+
+### `unsync` module
+
+The default single-threaded backend (`unsync::Slot`), plus an `error` module
+with `Error`/`Result`.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+`thiserror`. No async, no GPU.
+
+## Usage
+
+Application code does not use `slot` directly — `xui::state` uses it to back
+hook scratch storage. The interesting property is the phase discipline: it
+prevents reading hook state outside a render pass and writing it outside the
+event/effect phases, catching a whole class of bugs in debug builds.

diff --git a/docs/crates/xui-animation.md b/docs/crates/xui-animation.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..404562c
--- a/docs/crates/xui-animation.md
+++ b/docs/crates/xui-animation.md
@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+# `xui-animation` — animation primitives
+
+Timing and interpolation primitives shared by the style pipeline and component
+animations. It re-exports `Easing`, `Transition`, and `AnimationProgress` from
+`xui-interface` and adds the `Animatable` trait, derive, and `Tween`/`Timeline`
+helpers.
+
+## Public API
+
+### `Animatable` trait + derive
+
+```rust
+pub trait Animatable: Sized {
+    fn interpolate(from: &Self, to: &Self, progress: f32) -> Self;
+}
+```
+
+Derived field-wise for structs via `#[derive(Animatable)]` (provided by
+`xui-macros`). Generic structs get per-field `T: Animatable` bounds.
+
+Built-in impls:
+
+- `f32`, `ordered_float::NotNan<f32>`
+- `Point`, `Size<f32>`, `EdgeInsets`
+- `Color` (linear RGBA mix via `palette`)
+- `LengthValue`, `Sizing` (percent/fix interpolate; other variant pairs snap)
+- `ColorValue`, `ColorStyle` (solid & gradient variants; mismatched variants snap)
+- `LinearGradientStyle`, `RadialGradientStyle`
+- `ShadowStyle`, `StrokeStyle`, `ScrollbarStyle`
+- `Option<T: Animatable>`
+
+**Discrete rule:** when two values are different enum variants (or otherwise
+not interpolatable), the result snaps to `from` until `progress >= 1.0`, then
+to `to`.
+
+### `Tween<T: Animatable>` / `PropertyAnimation<T>`
+
+```rust
+let tween = Tween::new(0.0_f32, 10.0,
+    Transition::new(Duration::from_millis(100)).ease(Easing::Linear));
+tween.sample(Duration::from_millis(50));     // 5.0
+tween.sample_progress(0.25);                 // applies easing then interpolates
+```
+
+### `Timeline`
+
+Wraps a `Transition` and an `AnimationClock`. `tick(delta)` advances the clock
+and returns the current `AnimationProgress`; `progress()` reads without
+advancing; `reset()` zeroes the clock.
+
+### `AnimationClock`
+
+A simple monotonic `Duration` accumulator: `tick`, `set_elapsed`, `elapsed`,
+`reset`.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+`palette` (color mix), `xui-interface` (types + `Transition`/`Easing`),
+`xui-macros` (derive), `ordered-float`.
+
+## Usage
+
+```rust
+use xui_animation::{Animatable, Tween};
+use xui_interface::{Color, Easing, Transition, Point};
+use std::time::Duration;
+
+#[derive(Animatable)]
+struct Motion { position: Point, opacity: f32 }
+
+let m = Motion::interpolate(
+    &Motion { position: Point::new(0.0, 10.0), opacity: 0.2 },
+    &Motion { position: Point::new(10.0, 30.0), opacity: 0.8 },
+    0.5,
+);
+// position == (5.0, 20.0), opacity == 0.5
+```

diff --git a/docs/crates/xui-assets.md b/docs/crates/xui-assets.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7d1ce4f
--- a/docs/crates/xui-assets.md
+++ b/docs/crates/xui-assets.md
@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+# `xui-assets` — source mounting and caching
+
+The runtime side of the asset system. An `AssetManager` mounts one or more
+`AssetSource`s and resolves assets by `AssetId`, caching decompressed immutable
+bytes and parsing them through pluggable `AssetFormat`s. It re-exports the
+container types from [`xui-pak`](xui-pak.md).
+
+## Public API
+
+### `AssetManager`
+
+- `new()` / `with_cache_capacity(capacity)` / `Default`.
+- `mount(source)` / `mount_arc(arc)` — append a source at the lowest priority.
+  Sources are searched in **insertion order; first match wins** (mount
+  high-priority overlays first).
+- `metadata(id)` / `metadata_path(path)` / `load(id)` / `load_path(path)`.
+- `read::<F: AssetFormat>(id)` / `read_path::<F>(path)` — load + parse; errors
+  carry the offending asset path.
+- `invalidate_cache()` — drop cached decompressed bytes.
+
+### `AssetFormat` trait
+
+Decouples parsing policy from the source and the produced value:
+
+```rust
+pub trait AssetFormat {
+    type Output;
+    type Error: Error + Send + Sync + 'static;
+    fn parse(data: AssetData) -> Result<Self::Output, Self::Error>;
+}
+```
+
+Downstream crates implement `AssetFormat` for image/font/audio types they own.
+
+### `DirectorySource`
+
+A `Volatile` source backed by a real directory. It re-scans on each lookup
+(slower, but live edits are picked up), hashes content with `blake3`, and
+serves bytes as `AssetBytes::Owned`. Intended for development; immutable
+release content should use an indexed PAK.
+
+### Errors
+
+`AssetReadError` (`Load(AssetError)` or `Parse { path, source }`).
+
+### Re-exports from `xui-pak`
+
+`AssetBytes`, `AssetData`, `AssetError`, `AssetId`, `AssetMetadata`,
+`AssetSource`, `CachePolicy`, `Compression`, `EmbeddedPak`, `PakOpenOptions`,
+`PakSource`, `normalize_asset_path`.
+
+## Cache behavior
+
+- `CachePolicy::Immutable` (paks): decompressed bytes are cached by
+  `(mount, id, content_hash)`. Uncompressed mapped/static assets stay zero-copy
+  (`AssetBytes::Mapped` / `Static`); compressed ones are decoded once and
+  cached as `AssetBytes::Owned`.
+- `CachePolicy::Volatile` (directory): never cached; always re-read so edits
+  take effect immediately.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+`xui-pak`, `moka` (sync cache), `ignore` (directory walk), `camino`, `blake3`,
+`thiserror`.
+
+## Usage
+
+Most apps get an `AssetManager` from the bootstrap module generated by
+[`cargo xui`](xui-cli.md):
+
+```rust
+// produced by xui::include_assets!()
+pub mod xui_assets {
+    pub mod refs { /* AssetId constants */ }
+    pub fn manager() -> Result<xui::assets::AssetManager, xui::assets::AssetError> { /* … */ }
+}
+
+let manager = xui_assets::manager()?;
+let bytes = manager.load_path("icons/app.png")?.unwrap();
+```
+
+For ad-hoc mounting:
+
+```rust
+use xui_assets::{AssetManager, DirectorySource, PakSource};
+
+let mut assets = AssetManager::new();
+assets.mount(DirectorySource::new("overlay")?);   // wins first
+assets.mount(PakSource::open("base.xpak")?);
+```

diff --git a/docs/crates/xui-cli.md b/docs/crates/xui-cli.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..523d9f2
--- a/docs/crates/xui-cli.md
+++ b/docs/crates/xui-cli.md
@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+# `xui-cli` — `cargo xui` subcommand
+
+The primary build tool for `xui` applications. `cargo xui` reads `xui.toml`
+next to the app's `Cargo.toml`, packs its assets into a deterministic `.xpak`,
+generates a bootstrap module, and then invokes Cargo with the
+`XUI_ASSETS_BOOTSTRAP` env var set so `xui::include_assets!()` can find it.
+
+## Binary
+
+`cargo-xui` (`xui-cli/src/main.rs`).
+
+## Commands
+
+```sh
+cargo xui build [cargo-args]        # build with generated assets
+cargo xui run   [cargo-args]        # run with generated assets
+cargo xui check [cargo-args]        # check with generated assets
+cargo xui test  [cargo-args]        # test with generated assets
+cargo xui clippy [cargo-args]       # clippy with generated assets
+cargo xui assets pack   [cargo-args]  # build the .xpak and report
+cargo xui assets list   [cargo-args]  # list entries in the .xpak
+cargo xui assets verify [cargo-args] # verify entry hashes
+```
+
+`cargo-args` are forwarded verbatim to Cargo (including `--release`,
+`--target`, `--manifest-path`, and a trailing `-- <args>` separator). Profile
+detection (`--release` / `--profile=…`) routes generated artifacts to the right
+`target/xui/<profile>/` directory. `--target` and `--target-dir` are honored.
+
+## `xui.toml`
+
+```toml
+[assets]
+source = "assets"           # directory scanned for assets
+bundle = "embedded"          # "embedded" (include_bytes!) or "external" (ship beside exe)
+dev_directory = true         # mount the source dir live during dev runs
+output = "assets.xpak"
+compression_level = 3
+
+[[assets.rules]]
+glob = "**/*.{png,jpg,ogg,mp4,zip}"
+compression = "none"
+alignment = 16
+
+[[assets.rules]]
+glob = "**/*"
+compression = "zstd"
+alignment = 1
+```
+
+## What `cargo xui` does
+
+1. Resolve the manifest (from `--manifest-path` or the current directory).
+2. Parse `xui.toml` and run `cargo metadata` to find the target directory.
+3. Build the `.xpak` and `xui_asset_refs.rs` into
+   `<target>/xui/<profile>/` via [`xui-pak-build`](xui-pak-build.md).
+4. Write a bootstrap module (`xui_assets_bootstrap.rs`) exposing
+   `xui_assets::refs` and `xui_assets::manager()`. The `manager()` mounts:
+   - `DirectorySource(source)` first, when `dev_directory = true` (live edits);
+   - `EmbeddedPak(include_bytes!(pak))` (embedded mode) **or**
+     `PakSource::open(pak)` (external mode, copying the `.xpak` next to the
+     executable).
+5. Set `XUI_ASSETS_BOOTSTRAP` to the bootstrap path and invoke Cargo.
+
+## Library API
+
+`xui_cli::run(args) -> Result<(), CliError>` — entry point used by the binary;
+also callable directly. `CliError` carries `print()` / `exit_code()`.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+`clap` (derive), `camino`, `serde`/`serde_json`/`toml`, `thiserror`,
+`xui-pak`, `xui-pak-build`.
+
+## Installation
+
+```sh
+cargo install --path xui-cli
+```
+
+See the workspace [README](../../README.md#quick-start) for an end-to-end
+example, and [`xui-assets`](xui-assets.md) for how the generated `manager()`
+works at runtime.

