@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# `xui-macros` — procedural macros
+
+The compile-time DSLs that turn declarative markup and annotated functions into
+the runtime's `ElementDesc` / `Style` / component handles. A `proc-macro` crate.
+
+## Macros
+
+### `xui!` — element DSL
+
+JSX-like element syntax that produces an `xui::ElementDesc`.
+
+```rust
+let el: ElementDesc = xui! {
+    <Column style={style!(gap: 8.0, padding: 16.0)}>
+        <text style={style!(font_size: 24.0)}>{format!("count = {n}")}</text>
+        {other_child}
+    </Column>
+};
+```
+
+- Tags map to component functions or widget constructors.
+- Attribute values are arbitrary Rust expressions.
+- Children are elements or expressions yielding `ElementDesc`/`IntoChildren`.
+- Self-closing (`<Tag />`) and nested forms are supported.
+
+### `style!` — style builder with state rules
+
+Produces an `xui::Style`. Supports conditional (`if`) values over the widget
+state flags `hovered`, `pressed`, `focused`, `disabled`, `selected`, `checked`,
+`dragging`, combined with `&&`, `||`, and `!`. Conditions are lowered to
+`WidgetStateMatcher` rules at compile time; non-state `if` conditions fall
+through as ordinary runtime expressions.
+
+```rust
+let s = style!(
+    padding: 16.0,
+    background: if hovered { Color::WHITE } else { Color::BLACK },
+    border_width: if pressed || hovered { 2.0 } else { 1.0 },
+);
+```
+
+### `#[component]` / `component_fn!`
+
+Annotates a function that takes `&mut HookContext` (optional, inferred if
+absent) followed by named `&T` props. For each component the macro generates:
+
+- a hidden support module (`__xui_<Name>`),
+- a `<Name>Props` struct (when there is at least one prop),
+- a typestate `Builder` with required/optional setters and `#[defaults(...)]`
+  defaults (`children` defaults to an empty `Vec`),
+- `<Name>Props: WithChildren` when a `children` prop exists,
+- `<name>_component`, `<name>_component_type`, `<name>_component_render`,
+- public re-exports of the render handle and the function.
+
+```rust
+#[xui::component]
+#[defaults(padding = EdgeInsets::all(8.0))]
+fn card(cx: &mut HookContext, label: &str, padding: &EdgeInsets) -> ElementDesc {
+    xui! { <text style={style!(padding: *padding)}>{label}</text> }
+}
+
+// call site
+let el = xui! { <card label={"hi"} /> };
+```
+
+`component_fn!` expands one or more functions in a single block (useful when the
+same module defines several components).
+
+### `#[main]`
+
+Wraps `fn main()`. Before the user's body runs it:
+
+1. `include!`s the bootstrap module located at `$XUI_ASSETS_BOOTSTRAP`
+   (generated by `cargo xui`). Without that env var it emits a
+   `compile_error!("XUI assets require building through cargo xui")`.
+2. Calls `xui_assets::manager()` and installs the result into the process-global
+   `AssetManager` (or clears it on error).
+
+### `#[derive(Animatable)]`
+
+Field-wise `Animatable` impl for structs (named, tuple, unit, generic). Adds a
+`where T: Animatable` bound per field type. See [`xui-animation`](xui-animation.md).
+
+### `#[defaults]`
+
+Helper attribute consumed by `#[component]` to declare default prop values:
+`#[defaults(name = expr, other = expr)]`. Must not be used to give the `cx`
+parameter a default.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+`proc-macro2`, `proc-macro-crate`, `quote`, `syn` (`full`). The crate locates
+`xui` and `xui-animation` via `proc-macro-crate` so it works whether the
+consumer is `xui` itself or a downstream crate.

