+# `xui-pak-cli` — `xpak` binary
+
+A minimal, dependency-light CLI for inspecting and building `.xpak` archives
+without going through Cargo. It is the lower-level counterpart to
+[`cargo xui`](xui-cli.md); applications usually use `cargo xui` instead.
+
+## Binary
+
+`xpak` (`xui-pak-cli/src/main.rs`).
+
+## Commands
+
+```sh
+xpak pack [config] [output]   # build an .xpak from a config TOML (default: xui-pak.toml)
+xpak list <pak>                # list entries: original_len  stored_len  compression  path
+xpak verify <pak>              # verify every entry's content hash
+```
+
+`pack` delegates to
+[`xui_pak_build::build_from_config_to`](xui-pak-build.md); `list` and `verify`
+open the archive with [`xui_pak::PakSource`](xui-pak.md) and either iterate
+`entries()` or run `verify_all()`.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+Only `xui-pak` and `xui-pak-build` (plus their transitive deps). Intentionally
+no clap — argument parsing is hand-rolled to keep the binary tiny.
+
+## When to use it
+
+- Inspecting a built `.xpak` from a shell or script.
+- Building an archive from a custom config outside a Cargo workspace.
+- Verifying integrity in CI.
+
+For the full project workflow (config from `xui.toml`, embedded/external
+bundle modes, dev directory mounts, and invoking Cargo), use
+[`cargo xui`](xui-cli.md) instead.

