new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8eea160
--- a/docs/crates/xui-pak.md
+++ b/docs/crates/xui-pak.md
@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@
+# `xui-pak` — `.xpak` container format
+
+Versioned, deterministic containers for arbitrary application bytes. Defines the
+on-disk format, the `AssetSource` trait, and readers for mapped (file) and
+embedded (static slice) archives. No build logic lives here — see
+[`xui-pak-build`](xui-pak-build.md).
+
+## Format
+
+```text
++------------------- fixed 56-byte header ------------------+
+| MAGIC "XPAK" | version u16 | flags u16 | index_off u64 |
+| index_len u64 | index_hash [u8;32]                     |
++----------------------------------------------------------+
+| payload blobs (zstd-compressed or raw), aligned to 2^N |
++----------------------------------------------------------+
+| postcard index: PakIndex { entries: Vec<PakIndexEntry> } |
++----------------------------------------------------------+
+```
+
+- `MAGIC = *b"XPAK"`, `FORMAT_VERSION = 1`, `HEADER_LEN = 56`.
+- Each `PakIndexEntry` records `AssetId` (blake3 of the normalized path, first
+  16 bytes), path, content_hash (`[u8;32]`), offset, stored_len,
+  original_len, `Compression` (`None`/`Zstd`), and a power-of-two `alignment`.
+- The index is `postcard`-encoded and protected by its own blake3 hash in the
+  header. Entries are strictly sorted by `AssetId`.
+
+## Public API
+
+### Identifiers and metadata
+
+- `AssetId([u8;16])` — `from_bytes`, `as_bytes`, `from_path`, `from_normalized_path`.
+- `AssetMetadata` — id, path, content_hash, stored_len, original_len,
+  compression, alignment.
+- `Compression` — `None` | `Zstd`.
+- `CachePolicy` — `Immutable` | `Volatile` (used by sources, e.g.
+  [`xui-assets`](xui-assets.md)).
+- `normalize_asset_path(path) -> Result<Utf8PathBuf, AssetError>` — canonical,
+  forward-slash, no `..`/`.`/empty segments, no absolute paths.
+
+### Asset bytes
+
+`AssetBytes` — `Static { bytes, range }` (zero-copy from a static slice),
+`Mapped { map, range }` (zero-copy from an `Mmap`), or `Owned(Arc<[u8]>)`
+(decompressed). Implements `AsRef<[u8]>` / `Deref`.
+
+`AssetData { id, metadata, bytes }`, `AssetSource` trait (`metadata`, `load`,
+optional `cache_policy`).
+
+### Readers
+
+- `PakSource` — `open(path)` / `open_with_options`, backed by `Mmap`.
+  `entries()` iterator + `verify_all()`.
+- `EmbeddedPak` — `new(&'static [u8])` / `new_with_options`, zero-copy static.
+- `PakOpenOptions { max_index_size, max_decompressed_entry_size }` — hard
+  limits enforced on open/load (defense in depth).
+
+Both implement `AssetSource`.
+
+### `AssetError`
+
+`InvalidPath`, `InvalidPak`, `UnsupportedVersion`, `LimitExceeded`,
+`HashMismatch`, `Io`, `IndexDecode`.
+
+### `format` (doc-hidden)
+
+The header encoder/decoder and `PakIndex`/`PakIndexEntry` structs used by the
+build crate.
+
+## Validation
+
+The reader validates on open: header magic/version/flags, index range inside
+the file, index hash, strict `AssetId` sort order, no duplicate paths/ids,
+per-entry alignment/offset bounds, no payload/header/index overlap, and
+uncompressed length consistency. `load` re-verifies each entry's content hash.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+`blake3` (ids + integrity), `camino` (UTF-8 paths), `memmap2` (mapped reads),
+`postcard` (index serde), `serde`, `thiserror`, `zstd` (decompression).
+
+## Usage
+
+```rust
+use xui_pak::{AssetSource, PakSource};
+
+let pak = PakSource::open("assets.xpak")?;
+let id = xui_pak::AssetId::from_path("icons/app.png")?;
+if let Some(data) = pak.load(id)? {
+    assert_eq!(&*data.bytes, b"...");
+}
+pak.verify_all()?; // integrity-check every entry
+```

