index 0000000..7910b77
--- a/docs/crates/xui-slot.md
+++ b/docs/crates/xui-slot.md
@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+# `xui-slot` — generational box state
+
+A `Copy`-able `GenerationalBox<T>` state primitive with reference counting and
+an `Owner` that drops everything it created. Provides both unsync
+(single-threaded) and sync (thread-safe) backends. Conceptually a focused
+re-implementation of the generational-box pattern used for fine-grained,
+refcounted reactive state.
+
+## Public API
+
+### `GenerationalBox<T, S = UnsyncStorage>`
+
+The core `Copy` state handle. Behind a generation, so stale handles fail to
+read rather than aliasing freed memory.
+
+- `leak(value, location)` / `leak_rc(value, location)` — create with no owner
+  (manual drop required).
+- `try_read() -> Result<S::Ref<'static, T>, BorrowError>` / `read()` (panics).
+- `try_write() -> Result<S::Mut<'static, T>, BorrowMutError>` / `write()` /
+  `set(value)`.
+- `manually_drop()` — drop the value and invalidate the box.
+- `leak_reference() -> Result<GenerationalBox<T, S>>` — refcount-bump.
+- `point_to(other)` — retarget this box to another.
+- `ptr_eq`, `id() -> GenerationalBoxId`, `created_at()` (debug only),
+  `raw_ptr()`.
+
+### `Owner<S>`
+
+A refcounted guard (cloneable, `Default = S::owner()`). Anything it inserts is
+dropped when the last clone is dropped.
+
+- `insert(value) -> GenerationalBox<T, S>`
+- `insert_rc(value)` — refcounted box.
+- `insert_reference(other)` — add a reference to an existing box.
+- `insert_with_caller` / `insert_rc_with_caller` — blame a specific
+  `&'static Location` (used by macros for better panic messages).
+
+### Storages
+
+- `UnsyncStorage` — `RefCell`-backed; panics on borrow-while-borrowed.
+- `SyncStorage` — `RwLock`-backed; `Send` + `Sync`.
+- `Storage<Data>` trait — `try_read` / `try_write` / `new` / `new_rc` /
+  `new_reference` / `change_reference`.
+- `AnyStorage` trait — reference/mapping helpers (`map`/`try_map` for both
+  `Ref`/`Mut`), `downcast_lifetime_ref`/`_mut`, `data_ptr`, `recycle`, `owner`.
+
+### Ids and errors
+
+`GenerationalBoxId` (`Send`/`Sync`, type-erased), `GenerationalPointer<S>`.
+`BorrowError` / `BorrowMutError` / `BorrowResult` (in `error`/`references`).
+
+## Module map
+
+`error`, `entry`, `references`, `sync` (`SyncStorage`), `unsync`
+(`UnsyncStorage`).
+
+## Dependencies
+
+`parking_lot` (sync storage lock), `tracing`. No GPU, no async runtime.
+
+## Usage
+
+```rust
+use xui_slot::{Owner, UnsyncStorage};
+
+let owner: Owner = Owner::default();
+let a = owner.insert(42_i32);
+assert_eq!(*a.read(), 42);
+*a.write() = 7;
+assert_eq!(*a.read(), 7);
+// dropping `owner` invalidates `a`.
+```
+
+Most consumers reach this indirectly through `xui::state` hooks; it is exposed
+for crates that want the same fine-grained, owner-scoped state semantics
+outside the `xui` runtime.

