--- a/docs/crates/xui-text-engine.md
+++ b/docs/crates/xui-text-engine.md
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# `xui-text-engine` — `cosmic-text` text backend
+
+A concrete implementation of the `xui_interface::text` traits
+(`TextBackend`, `Shaper`, `FontDatabase`, `GlyphRasterizer`) backed by the
+[`cosmic-text`](https://docs.rs/cosmic-text) crate. This is the default text
+backend used by `xui` applications.
+
+## Public API
+
+### `CosmicEngine`
+
+The single entry point. Owns a `cosmic_text::FontSystem`, a `SwashCache`, a
+font epoch, and a scale factor.
+
+- `CosmicEngine::new(init_scale_factor: f32)` — `Default` uses `1.0`.
+- `font_system()` / `font_system_mut()` (mutating bumps the epoch so caches
+  invalidate), `swash_cache()` / `swash_cache_mut()`.
+- Implements `Shaper::layout_paragraph` by driving a reused `Buffer` through
+  cosmic-text shaping, then translating cosmic runs into the
+  `ParagraphLayout<fontdb::ID, CacheKey>` shape expected by the framework
+  (lines, runs, glyphs, clusters, each with text ranges and hitboxes).
+- Implements `FontDatabase` (`epoch`, `load_system_fonts`, `load_font_bytes`,
+  `query`, `font_data` returning a `FontDataRef`).
+- Implements `GlyphRasterizer::rasterize` via `SwashCache::get_image`, producing
+  `RasterizedGlyph` with `Mask` / `SubpixelMask` / `Color` formats.
+
+### `CosmicParagraphState`
+
+`Default`; caches a reusable `Buffer` between layouts so repeated frames avoid
+re-allocation.
+
+## Style mapping
+
+`xui-interface` paragraph/text-box options map onto cosmic-text:
+
+- `TextAlign` → cosmic `Align` (`Start` stays default; `Center`/`End`/`Justify`).
+- `WhiteSpace` + `OverflowWrap` → `Wrap` (`None`/`Word`/`Glyph`/`WordOrGlyph`).
+- `TextOverflow::{Clip,Ellipsis}` × `max_lines` → cosmic `Ellipsize`.
+- `max_lines == Some(0)` short-circuits to an empty layout.
+- `FontWeight`, `FontStyle`, `FontStretch`, `FontFamily`, `LineHeight`,
+  underline decoration are mapped to cosmic `Attrs`/`fontdb::Query`.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+`cosmic-text`, `xui-interface`.
+
+## Usage
+
+Usually selected automatically by the runtime. To construct one explicitly:
+
+```rust
+use xui_text_engine::CosmicEngine;
+let mut engine = CosmicEngine::new(1.0); // scale factor for HiDPI
+engine.load_system_fonts();
+```

