@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# `xui-winit` — `winit` window and event-loop integration
+
+Glues an `xui::app::App` to a `winit` window and an optional render backend.
+Translates raw `winit` events into `xui_interface::events::RawEvent`s and drives
+the `GuiRuntime`. Feature flags select the backend.
+
+## Feature flags
+
+```toml
+[dependencies]
+xui-winit = { path = "../xui-winit", features = ["skia"] }   # default
+# or
+xui-winit = { path = "../xui-winit", default-features = false, features = ["wgpu"] }
+```
+
+- `skia` (default) — pulls in [`xui-skia`](xui-skia.md) and re-exports
+  `SkiaBackend`, `SkiaTextBackend`, and the Skia text/cache types. Enables the
+  `runner` function.
+- `wgpu` — enables the optional `wgpu` renderer module: `WGPUBackend`,
+  `WgpuBackendOptions`, `WgpuBackendInitError`, plus a `TexturePool` /
+  `TextureLease` / `TexturePoolStats` texture-lifecycle subsystem.
+
+## Public API
+
+### Runner
+
+- `runner(app, options) -> Result<(), WinitRunError>` — **`skia` feature only.**
+  Creates the window, builds a `SkiaBackend`, and runs the event loop.
+- `WinitRunner` — lower-level runner you can drive yourself.
+- `WinitRunnerOptions` — window/backend options.
+- `WinitBackendInitError`, `WinitRunError`.
+
+### Event translation
+
+`translate_window_event`, `translate_mouse_button`, `translate_mouse_wheel`,
+`translate_named_key`, `translate_physical_key`.
+
+### SDF shader
+
+`UI_SHADER_WGSL` — the WGSL shader source used by the `wgpu` path.
+
+## Modules
+
+`device` (input device state), `error`, `runner` (the loop), `sdf` (shader),
+`translate` (event mapping). The `wgpu` feature adds `wgpu` and `renders`.
+
+## Dependencies
+
+`winit`, `xui`, `xui-render-graph`, `xui-interface`, `xui-text-engine`,
+`bytemuck`. `skia` feature: `xui-skia`. `wgpu` feature: `wgpu`,
+`etagere`, `pollster`.
+
+## Usage
+
+```rust
+use xui::prelude::*;
+use xui_winit::{runner, WinitRunnerOptions};
+
+#[xui::main]
+fn main() {
+    xui::include_assets!();
+    let app = App::new(root_component);
+    runner(app, WinitRunnerOptions::default()).expect("failed to run");
+}
+```
+
+See [`xui-example-app`](xui-example-app.md) for the full setup.

